Note on the plant data (source/*.json, dist/*.json)

The descriptions, care tips, watering intervals, and light/humidity/temperature
preferences are original editorial content and are covered by the license above,
as are the schema, the category system, and the translations. Scientific names
follow the accepted names in Plants of the World Online (POWO, Royal Botanic
Gardens, Kew), toxicity classifications are aligned with the ASPCA toxic and
non-toxic plant lists, and hardiness zones follow the USDA scale; those sources
are cited, not reproduced. Individual facts (a species name, a hardiness zone)
are not themselves copyrightable; the license applies to this particular curated
compilation and its presentation.

The dataset is provided for general information only and is not a substitute
for professional horticultural, botanical, or veterinary advice.
